---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Base title={`About | ${site.name}`}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />
  <h1 class="mt-1 font-display text-[44px] leading-none font-bold text-balance">Good training, no coach.</h1>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Open Training is for players who know the basics and want to get better, but have no coach and don't know what to practice. It gives you ready-made practice for the court. Pick a goal, like getting to the kitchen or winning the dink battle, and you get a 30-minute session of three drills that build on each other. Or pick a single shot, like the drop or the volley, and you get drills that repeat only that shot, from slow to
    full pace. Every drill comes with a short video that shows how it is played.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">The system behind it</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Every session is built so you learn the shot by playing it, not by being told. Behind that is a training system,
    made from more than 200 reviewed YouTube videos by coaches and pros. AI helped turn the videos into drills and sessions, and I
    decide which ones go online. The video for a drill starts right where the drill is shown.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2">
    A session climbs in three steps, based on sports-science research on how players learn best: find the shot, add
    pressure, then play it in a real point. Along the way, simple rules like a target zone or a limit on shots make
    sure the shot you want to learn is the one that wins the point. Aim for about seven good shots out of ten.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2">
    You don't have to study the system to use it: pick a goal or a shot, and the site picks the drills for you. If you want to see the whole system, the
    overview lays it out.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2"><a href="/overview/" data-overview-link class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center font-head font-bold underline underline-offset-4">See the Training System Overview →</a></p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">Non-commercial</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Open Training is a private, non-commercial project by Volker Max Meyer, a pickleball player in Berlin. No club or
    company runs it. There are no ads and no sign-up, and nothing is for sale. I want to help players get better and
    bring pickleball to the people.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">Feedback welcome</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Open Training is a work in progress. I add and change sessions and drills based on what players tell me. After a goal
    session, the short form at the end is the quickest way. For a shot drill, a missing drill or anything else, just email
    me at {site.contactEmail}.
  </p>
</Base>
